  "description": "Band-pass filtered (1-250 Hz) epidural ECoG recordings from a single participant with incomplete tetraplegia, implanted with the chronic wireless WIMAGINE device over left primary motor and sensory cortex. The participant executed or imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, singly or simultaneously, across eight sessions. The dataset supports study of how simultaneous motor imagination and execution can be decoupled via orthogonal neural representations, and is a BIDS derivative repackaging of the authors' Zenodo release.",
  "methods_description": "Thirty-two ECoG channels were recorded at about 585 Hz with the WIMAGINE wireless epidural implant while the participant, seated in front of a screen with instructions and a progress bar, executed or imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, singly or simultaneously. EMG of the extensor digitorum and lateral deltoid monitored execution. The authors applied a zero-phase 5th-order Butterworth band-pass filter (1-250 Hz) to each run.",
